        {
          "id": "0bce8a18-6f30-3360-a21d-c3cd49cbc4d9",
          "content": {
            "id": "0bce8a18-6f30-3360-a21d-c3cd49cbc4d9",
            "contentType": "VIDEO",
            "title": "Waymo\u2019s new Zeekr robotaxi seen testing in San Diego",
            "description": "<title><body><p>STORY: :: San Diego, California</p><p>:: November 19, 2025</p><p>:: Waymo\u2019s new Zeekr robotaxi is spotted testing in San Diego before services start in the city next year</p><p>:: The vehicle developed with Chinese automaker Geely is part of Waymo\u2019s expansion to Las Vegas, San Diego and Detroit</p><p>Waymo announced in early November it will launch its robotaxi service in Las Vegas, San Diego and Detroit next year, marking its biggest geographic expansion yet.</p><p>The Alphabet unit will also start driving its new Zeekr-built vehicles, alongside its existing Jaguar I-PACE fleet, it added.</p><p>The new Zeekr model, developed with Chinese automaker Geely, are designed specifically for robotaxi use cases and will be rolled out gradually as the company expands its service.</p><p>Companies like Waymo, Tesla TSLA.O and Amazon's Zoox are investing billions into self-driving technology.</p><p>Tesla launched its long-awaited robotaxi service earlier this year, while Waymo already operates driverless services in Phoenix, San Francisco, Los Angeles, and Austin, and has completed more than 10 million trips.</p></body></title>",
            "summary": "<body><p>STORY: :: San Diego, California</p><p>:: November 19, 2025</p><p>:: Waymo\u2019s new Zeekr robotaxi is spotted testing in San Diego before services start in the city next year</p><p>:: The vehicle developed with Chinese automaker Geely is part of Waymo\u2019s expansion to Las Vegas, San Diego and Detroit</p><p>Waymo announced in early November it will launch its robotaxi service in Las Vegas, San Diego and Detroit next year, marking its biggest geographic expansion yet.</p><p>The Alphabet unit will also start driving its new Zeekr-built vehicles, alongside its existing Jaguar I-PACE fleet, it added.</p><p>The new Zeekr model, developed with Chinese automaker Geely, are designed specifically for robotaxi use cases and will be rolled out gradually as the company expands its service.</p><p>Companies like Waymo, Tesla TSLA.O and Amazon's Zoox are investing billions into self-driving technology.</p><p>Tesla launched its long-awaited robotaxi service earlier this year, while Waymo already operates driverless services in Phoenix, San Francisco, Los Angeles, and Austin, and has completed more than 10 million trips.</p></body>",
            "pubDate": "2025-11-20T08:43:24Z",
